      "side": 1,
      "message": "This comment implies that cables supporting neither PD 3.0/USB4 nor TBT3 will be treated as unidirectional. I don\u0027t think that would be appropriate, but the actual code on lines 848 and 849 appears to treat them as bidirectional by constructing a 0-valued tbt_mode_resp_cable and then reading the lsrx_comm bit, which happens to indicate bidirectional link training when it\u0027s 0.\n\nIt took me a while to piece that together, and I think that it would be helpful if\n1) this comment accurately reflected what the code was doing,\n2) it was placed right above the corresponding code, and\n3) it explained a little bit how the return value came to be.",
